◦ Clicking Open filtered data opens a table with the sorted data to be used for data fitting, i.e., after
eliminating unwanted values.
Once you have entered the required data or selected the required settings, you can proceed to the tab Fit.
Back to Distribution-Fitting with DataFit
Fit Data in DataFit
In this step we fit data in DataFit.
DataFit estimates the parameters of the selected distribution(s) and then performs a goodness-of-fit test
with the filtered data on the tab FIT.
• Click Select and select one, several or all distributions in the dialog that opens.
• Enter a Level of significance for the values. You can enter a number between 0 and 1. In most cases
you will enter a number between 0 and 0.2.
• Click Fit to estimate the parameters for the selected distribution or distributions using the sample.
• If you are investigating a large sample, you will have to use the Chi-Square Test is the Goodness-of-Fit
Test. For this you have to enter the Number of classes. The Goodness-of-Fit Test describes how good
the distribution with its parameters fits the given sample.
• Click Show to display a histogram of the sample in a chart.
Once you have entered the required data or selected the required settings, you can proceed to the tab
Evaluation.
Back to Distribution-Fitting with DataFit
